  <h2 style="font-size:22px;margin:0 0 6px">Start here: which form do you need?</h2>
  <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#39414B;margin:0 0 10px">Choosing the wrong form is one of the most common reasons a filing is rejected or dismissed without a judge reaching the substance. The short version:</p>
  <ul style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#39414B;margin:0 0 30px;padding-left:22px">
    <li><strong>Convicted in federal court, challenging the conviction or sentence itself</strong> &rarr; AO 243 (&sect; 2255), filed in the court that sentenced you.</li>
    <li><strong>Challenging how the Bureau of Prisons is carrying out your sentence</strong> &mdash; credits, computation, discipline &rarr; AO 242 (&sect; 2241), filed where you are confined.</li>
    <li><strong>In custody on a state court judgment, seeking federal review</strong> &rarr; AO 241 (&sect; 2254).</li>
    <li><strong>Suing over conditions or treatment rather than challenging custody</strong> &rarr; Pro Se 14 or 15 (civil rights complaint).</li>
    <li><strong>Cannot afford the costs</strong> &rarr; AO 240 or AO 239 (in forma pauperis), filed alongside the above.</li>
  </ul>

