  <h2 style="font-size:22px;margin:44px 0 6px">Before you file</h2>
  <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#39414B;margin:0 0 30px">Filling in a form correctly is only part of it. The AO 243 instructions, for example, note that <strong>no fee is required with a &sect; 2255 motion</strong>, that additional pages are not permitted except for the facts supporting your grounds, that only judgments from one court may be challenged in a single motion, and that the motion must be signed under penalty of perjury. Details like these decide filings more often than the underlying legal argument does.</p>

